# Enforcement paths (#235). The default ruleset has require_code_owner_review on, so a change to
# a path below needs a code-owner review and the App's APPROVE does not merge it alone. The only
# owner is the operator, who authors these pull requests and cannot approve them, so these merges
# go through the administrator bypass. That bypass skips only the default ruleset. The "CI
# required" ruleset has no bypass list, so its checks, code scanning, force-push and deletion
# rules still hold. Skills and patterns are deliberately not owned.
# Last match wins. No entry below overlaps another.
/.github/                                   @Cringely
/.gitattributes                             @Cringely
/core/claude/hooks/                         @Cringely
/core/claude/agents/                        @Cringely
/core/claude/templates/                     @Cringely
/install/                                   @Cringely
/tools/pr-review/                           @Cringely
/account/claude/rules/                      @Cringely
/account/claude/agents/                     @Cringely
/account/claude/hooks/                      @Cringely
/account/claude/tools/                      @Cringely
/account/claude/settings.account.json       @Cringely
/test/                                      @Cringely
